le":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T21:57:22-07:00","id":1139099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1137823-books-on-supernatural-stuff-do-people-keep-them-on-their-tablets-and-e-readersd?p=1138687#post1138687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">basicly<br /> <br /> though the prince or archbishop had best be notified, just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prince neither wants nor needs to be informed of it. Best case, you have a prince who just shrugs and goes 'what will these crazy neonates think of next! Stop texting me with every fucking detail of your day, I'm not Vampire Twitter.' More likely case, you have a prince or bishop who doesn't understand what exactly it means and may or may not react violently. Worst case, you have a prince who knows exactly what it means, doesn't like Noddists, and has you killed on principle for even <i>risking</i> the masquerade and for being a filthy Noddist.<br /> <br /> The Prince is not your supervisor. The Prince is not your buddy. Do not text the Prince with selfies unless they're really, really, really cool. Do not tweet <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6680-theprince\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6680\" data-vbnamecard=\"6680\">ThePrince</a>. Do not bother the Prince with trivialities. Do not tell the Prince when you are breaking a Tradition unless you need to run damage control and minimize the cost of it being revealed that you have.<br /> <br /> Remember - your average prince, even in America, is a century plus old bloodsucking monster who, more often than not, has literally murdered his way to the top of the local food chain or murdered dozens of men, women, and cainites in order to stay at it if they've been established for long. The same is true of your average Archbishop. They aren't your cool boss, they're a terrifying sociopath with the literal power of life and death over you, and they don't have a boss to reign them in unless you have some really powerful friends. If they want to have you dragged behind a tow-truck on a gravel road every night for two straight years, <i>they can</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 09-10-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T05:10:17-07:00","id":1139147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1137823-books-on-supernatural-stuff-do-people-keep-them-on-their-tablets-and-e-readersd?p=1139099#post1139099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Prince neither wants nor needs to be informed of it. Best case, you have a prince who just shrugs and goes 'what will these crazy neonates think of next! Stop texting me with every fucking detail of your day, I'm not Vampire Twitter.' More likely case, you have a prince or bishop who doesn't understand what exactly it means and may or may not react violently. Worst case, you have a prince who knows exactly what it means, doesn't like Noddists, and has you killed on principle for even <i>risking</i> the masquerade and for being a filthy Noddist.<br /> <br /> The Prince is not your supervisor. The Prince is not your buddy. Do not text the Prince with selfies unless they're really, really, really cool. Do not tweet <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6680-theprince\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6680\" data-vbnamecard=\"6680\">ThePrince</a>. Do not bother the Prince with trivialities. Do not tell the Prince when you are breaking a Tradition unless you need to run damage control and minimize the cost of it being revealed that you have.<br /> <br /> Remember - your average prince, even in America, is a century plus old bloodsucking monster who, more often than not, has literally murdered his way to the top of the local food chain or murdered dozens of men, women, and cainites in order to stay at it if they've been established for long. The same is true of your average Archbishop. They aren't your cool boss, they're a terrifying sociopath with the literal power of life and death over you, and they don't have a boss to reign them in unless you have some really powerful friends. If they want to have you dragged behind a tow-truck on a gravel road every night for two straight years, <i>they can</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then, what would you advise me to do, just to be on the safe side?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T07:02:17-07:00","id":1139173,"title":"","content":"Not load your ancient grimoires onto an electronic device at all, probably. There are several steps it can go horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> Step 1. Own the grimoire. Already, you're potentially in deep shit depending on what it is.<br /> <br /> Step 2. Digitize the grimoire. Either you're scanning it or typing it out by hand. Either one, depending on what exactly you are and what exactly you're using, might get picked up by all kinds of greeblies and goblins out there, from a keylogging russian scammer to a Pentex bane to a curious Glass Walker who gets a sudden twitching urge to poke his head in when he smells Digital Magic going on.<br /> <br /> Step 3. Encrypt the grimoire. This is where shit gets weird, because either you're using a conventional encryption - in which case, magic might snap it like a twig - or magic. If you're using magic, your run of the mill ipad probably doesn't come with Bloodcrypt+ pre-installed, so unless you have the nous to do it yourself, <i>someone</i> is going to know - and <i>someone</i> is going to have leverage over you forever. Worse yet, it might be more than one someone, since you're either using the kind of jailbroken extra functionality someone-in-the-know has to provide, or a device custom built using the kind of Special Components that probably get you added to a watchlist somewhere deep in the NWO, Pentex, or Glass Walkers computers. Either way, you're potentially fucked.<br /> <br /> Step 4. Cart around a sacred, rare, and/or literally magical text in your phone/ipad/laptop to read in public. Why? What advantage does it actually offer? Does that advantage offset the part where you're potentially carrying around a massive magnet for trouble from all kinds of sectors? If it has actual magic in it, then other vampires/garou/banes/mages/whatever have a strong reason to want to gank you for it. If it doesn't, then it's still potentially a walking secrecy breach for something that conveys basically no value to having on you in public.<br /> <br /> 99% of the time, there will be exactly no advantage to a digitized grimoire over a non-digitized one. Need it to do magic? Unless you find yourself in the very strange scenario of needing to consult grimoires quickly in the field all the time, you can probably just take the actual book when you need it. The situations where there is an advantage, a temporary copy is probably a better bet - e.g. showing proof you have those missing pages from the Book of Nod to a buyer without taking the actual thing. Unless security through obscurity is your bet, and you're keeping it on just one old hard drive among dozens lying around in the storage unit untouched for years at a time under a fake name, it's not going to be much use.<br /> <br /> Bottom line? If you have to worry about someone finding your actual Sinister Book, you've probably got way bigger problems in your unlife than how to digitize it. Like 'how did they get into my haven' and 'why aren't I dead yet?' The dangers are far less if a mortal finds it - 'huh, weird book' describes half my occult library - than another mage, cainite, or garou does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T10:49:49-07:00","id":1139227,"title":"","content":"I have books on Tarot Reading Japanese language, Shinto Worship, and a good deal of Genital integrity material on my E reader, that might raise some eyebrows, if it was ever searched, but I find it more convenient to keep it on there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T16:41:27-07:00","id":1139300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1137823-books-on-supernatural-stuff-do-people-keep-them-on-their-tablets-and-e-readersd?p=1139227#post1139227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have books on Tarot Reading Japanese language, Shinto Worship, and a good deal of Genital integrity material on my E reader, that might raise some eyebrows, if it was ever searched, but I find it more convenient to keep it on there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that none of those fall into the two following categories.<br /> 1. Material that is literally magical, and thus a magnet for other mages/vampires/garou/etc to try and take from you - assuming the magic can actually be digitized in the first place.<br /> 2. Material that is either so rare or so heretical that it could cost you your life if someone else found out you have it, either because they want it or because they don't want <i>you</i> to have it.<br /> <br /> All your stuff does is cause you <i>slight</i> embarassment. Tarot? Amateur hour wizardry that everyone's cousin dabbles in at least once. Japanese language? At worst, a snicker of 'weeb'. Shinto texts? Unless you live in a particularly repressive Islamic state, probably wouldn't even raise an eyebrow outside of all but the most close-minded. Anti-genital mutilation stuff? Not exactly Dangerous Sicko Pervert hour over there.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to 'that book that literally lets you summon The Great Satan to do your bidding' and 'that one book that, depending on the Prince, is either outright banned or strongly discouraged' and 'a sacred work that is <i>not</i> to be recorded any way but orally, whose existence in digitized form is thus blasphemy, and blasphemy towards creatures with giant teeth and lots of fur at that'. They're a whole <i>other</i> level of dangerous and controversial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T18:47:51-07:00","id":1139600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1137823-books-on-supernatural-stuff-do-people-keep-them-on-their-tablets-and-e-readersd?p=1139300#post1139300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that none of those fall into the two following categories.<br /> 1. Material that is literally magical, and thus a magnet for other mages/vampires/garou/etc to try and take from you - assuming the magic can actually be digitized in the first place.<br /> 2. Material that is either so rare or so heretical that it could cost you your life if someone else found out you have it, either because they want it or because they don't want <i>you</i> to have it.<br /> <br /> All your stuff does is cause you <i>slight</i> embarassment. Tarot? Amateur hour wizardry that everyone's cousin dabbles in at least once. Japanese language? At worst, a snicker of 'weeb'. Shinto texts? Unless you live in a particularly repressive Islamic state, probably wouldn't even raise an eyebrow outside of all but the most close-minded. Anti-genital mutilation stuff? Not exactly Dangerous Sicko Pervert hour over there.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to 'that book that literally lets you summon The Great Satan to do your bidding' and 'that one book that, depending on the Prince, is either outright banned or strongly discouraged' and 'a sacred work that is <i>not</i> to be recorded any way but orally, whose existence in digitized form is thus blasphemy, and blasphemy towards creatures with giant teeth and lots of fur at that'. They're a whole <i>other</i> level of dangerous and controversial.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Forgot to mention my Errotica, most of it focusing on DD (Wondered for a bit how common such relationships are in marriages between garou and kinfolk? Think it would be dangerous, by tempting Frenzy or...) <br /> <br /> <br /> but both the Errotica, and my Genital integrity stuff I keep digitalized largely to avoid weirding people out, any counters on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}